    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d170-a1">

                <pb facs="0259" n="139" xml:id="pg139"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Coolidge to Prince Ch’ing.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1905-03-06"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">March 6,
                    1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Imperial Highness</hi>: I have the honor to
                    state that I have this day received from the Department of State a print of a
                    recent correspondence between the Russian ambassador at Washington and the
                    Secretary of State, concerning the observance of neutrality by China in the
                    present war, together with the instructions sent to the American minister at
                    Peking on the subject and the reply of the Chinese Government.</p>
                <p>Having been instructed to transmit a copy of the same to your imperial highnesses
                    government, I have the honor to inclose one herein, and at the same time I take
                    the opportunity to renew, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Gardner
                    Coolidge.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
